## 9. Deliverables before you exit

Produce ALL of these. A story with good code and no deliverables is a story the
morning cannot use.

1. **Report section** — append your own section to
   `{{BASE}}/runtime/AUTOPILOT-REPORT.md`. Append, never rewrite: other stories
   own the sections above yours. Include: story id, PR number, merged or open,
   test command and counts, review rounds and final verdict, non-blocking
   findings, backlog row change, and anything the owner must look at.
2. **Handoff** — REWRITE `{{BASE}}/runtime/handoff/night-<id>.md`, YOUR story's
   own file, named for your queue id. At most 40 lines, in English: where this
   story stands, what is done, the EXACT next step, decisions and pitfalls,
   affected file paths, the worktree path and branch, and the park reason if you
   parked. Create the directory if missing:
   `mkdir -p {{BASE}}/runtime/handoff`.

   **The id is in the filename for a reason.** A single shared `night.md` is
   rewritten by every story of the night, so the last story to finish destroys
   every earlier story's parked resume state. Never write to `night.md`; never
   write, read or delete another story's `night-<other>.md`. If you parked, the
   next session resumes from `night-<id>.md` ALONE (section 3.1, case 1) — write
   it for someone who knows nothing. Only AFTER your own file is written you may
   overwrite `{{BASE}}/runtime/handoff/night-latest.md` with a one-line pointer
   (`{{RUN_DATE}} <id> — see night-<id>.md`) as a rolling index; it is NEVER a
   resume source and nothing reads state out of it.
3. **Decisions** — one `brain note decision: <decision and its reasoning>` call
   per non-trivial decision, in English, one decision per call.
4. **Machine note** — if you changed machine state at all:
   `update-monitor note "<one line, English>"`.
5. **The final line.** The very last line of your output, alone, exactly:

   ```
   RESULT <id> <merged|open|parked|blocked> PR#<n or -> review=<pass|parked> rounds=<n> reason=<review|timeout|context|ci|forbidden|merge-forbidden|tests|->
   ```

   - `<id>` is your queue id. `PR#-` when no PR was opened.
   - `review=pass` only when section 4 returned zero blocking findings WITH an
     evidence line. Otherwise `review=parked`.
   - `rounds=<n>` is the number of review rounds actually run.
   - `reason=` says WHY. It is exactly one token from this closed list, and
     every `parked` or `blocked` state MUST carry one of the real ones,
     and `merge-forbidden` is the one real token that goes with state `open`:

     | token       | when                                                        |
     |-------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
     | `review`    | blocking findings survived; an unmet `needs:` dependency; an empty or `-` acceptance-criteria cell; a closed decision you would have had to reopen |
     | `timeout`   | the FINALIZE instant at the top of this brief was reached    |
     | `context`   | the section 2 context threshold fired first                  |
     | `ci`        | the CI wait bound was reached with the run still queued or running |
     | `forbidden` | the story requires a change in a forbidden zone — section 1 or section 6 — so it is `blocked`, not parked |
     | `merge-forbidden` | the story is BOTH review-green and CI-green, but merging is not allowed — section 6 / `docs/NIGHT-RULES.md` forbids this session from merging (or the owner granted no merge for this project tonight). The PR is pushed, green and LEFT OPEN for the morning sweep; the state is `open`, `review=pass`, and nothing is merged. This is a SUCCESS, not a failure |
     | `tests`     | tests fail and cannot be made to pass without a forbidden route to green (section 4.4) |
     | `-`         | nothing was parked or blocked; valid ONLY with `merged`      |

     `parked ... reason=-` and `blocked ... reason=-` are malformed lines.
     `merge-forbidden` may never appear with `merged`: if you merged, merging
     was allowed. It carries state `open` and `review=pass`, never `blocked` —
     nothing about the story is broken, only the merge permission is absent.
   - Use this exact grammar everywhere the `RESULT` line appears: the top of
     this brief and sections 2, 4.5 and 8 all refer to the same line.
   - `merged` or `open` together with `review=parked` is a CONTRADICTION. Never
     emit it: if the review did not pass, the state is `parked` or `blocked`.
   - Write this line from evidence you verified yourself, never from an
     implementer sub-agent's claim.

